#%PAM-1.0
# reclogin's guest session. No password. Only the guest account. Only reclogin
# starts this service, and only when the Guest entry was chosen.
#
# Installed as /etc/pam.d/reclogin-guest on LevitateOS. The same lines as
# dist/pam/reclogin-guest.acornos (docs/reclogin-guest.md, point 4): the
# leading `-` skips a module that is not installed, so pam_systemd registers
# the session here and pam_elogind is skipped. reclogind checks after
# pam_open_session that the login service registered it (XDG_SESSION_ID)
# and refuses the guest otherwise. pam_limits reads
# /etc/security/limits.d/50-reclogin-guest.conf (nproc for the uid sweep).
# pam_nologin: /etc/nologin (or /run/nologin) keeps the guest out like
# everyone else. pam_keyinit force revoke: the guest's session gets a session
# keyring of its own (none of reclogind's is inherited) and it is revoked
# when the session closes; the guest's user keyrings are cleared by the
# cleanup's sweep.
auth      requisite  pam_succeed_if.so quiet user = guest
auth      required   pam_permit.so
account   requisite  pam_succeed_if.so quiet user = guest
account   required   pam_nologin.so
account   required   pam_permit.so
password  required   pam_deny.so
-session  optional   pam_keyinit.so force revoke
session   required   pam_limits.so
session   required   pam_unix.so
-session  optional   pam_systemd.so
-session  optional   pam_elogind.so
